# Every Dockerfile in this repo installs dependencies fresh inside the build
# stage. A local node_modules on the host is a different install — a
# different lockfile resolution, a different platform, a different point in
# time — and every `COPY <dir> <dir>` step in a Dockerfile blindly includes it
# if it exists, silently shadowing the correctly-installed one underneath.
# The failure this produces (a module resolves to a version that isn't in the
# image) has no stack trace pointing back here, so it stays ignored.
node_modules/
.next/
.turbo/
.pnpm-store/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

.git/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
